  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Ergebnisse durchgegangen und verglichen Für B entschieden. Im Vergleich ein geringer prozentualer Unterschied, was die Wahrscheinlichkeit betrifft' (Results reviewed and compared; decided for B. The comparison showed only a small percentage difference in probabilities). The individual considers the outcomes and compares the probabilities, noting a small difference. However, there is no mention of skewness, left-skewness, or any evaluation of the distribution of probabilities across favorable and unfavorable outcomes. The individual's justification centers only on the small difference in probabilities (0.1% vs. 0.2%), and the choice is made in favor of B, despite A having a higher probability of a positive outcome. No reference is made to the structure of the distribution or skewness of the lotteries.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the comparison of the proportion of probability on favorable outcomes — is not considered by the individual. The individual only notes a small difference in probabilities, without analyzing which lottery has more probability mass on the favorable outcome. The decision reason requires evaluating skewness (i.e., whether a greater portion of probability is on the favorable outcome), which is absent from the verbal report. The individual’s justification does not reference skewness or left-skewness at all. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual’s reasoning is based solely on a superficial comparison of probability percentages, not on the structural skewness of the lotteries. This indicates that the decision reason was not applied.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
