  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses on the size of the loss and the probability of loss occurring, not on the proportion of probability mass on favorable versus unfavorable outcomes. The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness — specifically, whether a lottery has more probability mass on favorable (0 Euro) outcomes compared to unfavorable (negative) outcomes — and preferring the more left-skewed one. A is more left-skewed (99.9% favorable, 0.1% unfavorable) than B (99.8% favorable, 0.2% unfavorable), so A should be preferred according to the reason. However, the individual chose B, and their justification is based on a smaller loss size, not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not reference skewness or distributional shape in their reasoning. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason.",
